        "net-overview-title": "TECHNICAL OVERVIEW",
        "net-overview-text": "Protocol: Sync is a research and development project on real-time multiplayer. It is a hub featuring several mini-games, built on a robust Client/Server architecture using ENet for the UDP transport layer.",
        "net-networking-title": "NETWORKING ARCHITECTURE",
        "net-net-1-title": "> GamePacket System",
        "net-net-1-desc": "Implementation of a binary serialization layer with <code><<</code> and <code>>></code> operator overloading. Automatic Endianness management (Big/Little) to ensure cross-platform data integrity.",
        "net-net-2-title": "> Client/Server Architecture",
        "net-net-2-desc": "State synchronization based on a server-authoritative model. Management of packet lifecycles (Ack), timeouts, and secure disconnections via a robust state machine.",
        "net-net-3-title": "> Multi-stream Management",
        "net-net-3-desc": "Leveraging ENet channels to eliminate 'Head-of-Line Blocking'. Strategic data distribution between reliable streams (system states) and unreliable sequenced streams (movements), ensuring maximum responsiveness.",
        "net-net-4-title": "> Prediction & Reconciliation",
        "net-net-4-desc": "Implementation of client-side prediction for instant control reactivity. Smooth reconciliation system correcting local position without jitter using an adaptive lerp based on <code>CORRECTION_STRENGTH</code>.",
